Show permanent popups as xdg_popups on webOS.

Firefox places noautohide panels (the add-on install prompt, among others)
directly instead of tracking them as popups. GTK then maps them as a plain
wl_subsurface, which the webOS compositor never displays, so the prompt
stayed invisible and add-ons could not be installed from addons.mozilla.org.
Track them like other popups: they become xdg_popups, which the webOS
adapter shows as its own subsurfaces and never dismisses on outside clicks.

diff --git a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
index 69ae6a6c20..c32b3c6af5 100644
--- a/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp
@@ -1397,8 +1397,13 @@ bool nsWindowWayland::WaylandPopupConfigure() {
   }
 
   // Popup state can be changed, see Bug 1728952.
-  bool permanentStateMatches =
-      mPopupTrackInHierarchy == !WaylandPopupIsPermanent();
+  // webOS: track permanent (noautohide) panels too. Untracked popups are
+  // placed directly, which GTK maps as a plain wl_subsurface, and the webOS
+  // compositor does not show those (the add-on install prompt stayed
+  // invisible). Tracked popups become xdg_popups, which the webOS adapter
+  // shows; it never dismisses popups on outside clicks, so panels that must
+  // stay open still do.
+  bool permanentStateMatches = mPopupTrackInHierarchy == true;
 
   // Popup permanent state (noautohide attribute) can change during popup life.
   if (mPopupTrackInHierarchyConfigured && permanentStateMatches) {
@@ -1429,7 +1434,7 @@ bool nsWindowWayland::WaylandPopupConfigure() {
     gtk_widget_unmap(mShell);
   }
 
-  mPopupTrackInHierarchy = !WaylandPopupIsPermanent();
+  mPopupTrackInHierarchy = true;
   LOG("  tracked in hierarchy %d\n", mPopupTrackInHierarchy);
 
   // See gdkwindow-wayland.c and
